WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.614 --> 00:00:27.995
Sign in and open the POS Terminal with your register already open.

2
00:00:28.095 --> 00:00:36.868
Add the products the customer is buying.

3
00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:42.281
If the customer has a coupon, type the code in the Coupon Code box under the cart.

4
00:00:42.381 --> 00:00:47.364
Select Apply. The discount comes off the total and the code shows as a chip.

5
00:00:50.492 --> 00:00:54.263
Select Pay Now. Besides Cash you can take Card or UPI.

6
00:00:54.363 --> 00:00:59.842
Choose Card. The received amount is filled in for you, so there is no change to give.

7
00:00:59.942 --> 00:01:06.270
UPI works the same way. Some methods also ask for a reference, such as a slip or transaction number.

8
00:01:06.382 --> 00:01:11.090
When the customer wants to pay with more than one method, choose Split.

9
00:01:11.196 --> 00:01:16.507
Each row is one method. Set the first to Cash and enter the part they pay in cash.

10
00:01:16.607 --> 00:01:23.458
The second row picks up what is still to pay. Set it to UPI and add the UPI reference. It shows Fully covered.

11
00:01:23.558 --> 00:01:27.823
Select Pay & Complete Sale to record both payments on one sale.

12
00:01:27.923 --> 00:01:31.920
The confirmation lists the payment methods that were used.

13
00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:39.250
A customer forgot their wallet? Add their items as normal.

14
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:44.550
Select Hold Sale. The cart is parked and the till is free for the next customer.

15
00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:49.190
Parked sales appear in the Held Sales list. The cart is empty again.

16
00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:54.160
When the customer is back, select Resume to bring the cart back as it was.

17
00:01:56.986 --> 00:02:02.628
From here you can take payment as usual. That is coupons, split payments and held sales.
